@startuml
title Unfracking: separating one policy out of a co-mingled UTxO
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EEF5FF
  BorderColor #4A78B5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #DCE9FA
  DiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
  ArrowColor #4A78B5
}

start
:holder owns a PLB UTxO carrying
policy A and the frozen policy F;
:build a transaction with
SpendViaUnfracking and the
unfracking withdraw-0;
if (acted policy's unfracking_logic_script set\nin its registry node?) then (no)
  :reject, an unset hook forbids
  unfracking for that policy;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
if (its withdraw-0 invoked in this transaction?) then (no)
  :reject;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
if (tx.mint is empty?) then (no)
  :reject, unfracking never mints or burns;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
if (every PLB input carries the same full address?) then (no)
  :reject, this is a transfer in disguise;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
if (owner authorised, signature or withdraw-0?) then (no)
  :reject;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
:per pair, keep address, datum, reference
script and every other policy byte-identical;
:strip the acted policy from the
continuing output entirely;
if (acted policy total on the owner's non-paired\noutputs equals the total on the inputs?) then (no)
  :reject, leak or fabrication;<<#FDEEEE>>
  stop
endif
:policy A now sits in its own UTxO,
free of the freeze on F;<<#E7F4EC>>
stop
@enduml
